{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["And the interpretation of <b>and Edom shall be a possession</b>: The downfall of Edom will be at the hand of the Messiah, for our exile today is considered to be at the hand of Rome, which is Edom, as it is said: \"The iniquity of the daughter of Zion is completed; He will no more exile you; He will punish your iniquity, O daughter of Edom; He will uncover your sins\" (Lamentations 4:22). And HaShem will not punish Edom until the iniquities of Zion are completed, at the time when He will no more exile them. Therefore Balaam mentioned Edom, for it is the one that contests our kingdom, and concerning it was said \"and one nation shall be stronger than the other nation\" (Genesis 25:23) — he prophesies that Edom will not fall completely until the time of the end, at the hand of the star that treads. And the interpretation of <b>and Seir shall be a possession of his enemies</b>: that Seir shall be a possession for his enemies; or \"his enemies\" are Edom and Seir, the ones mentioned, who are the enemies of Jacob, and they shall be a possession."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {0 "The verse citations from Lamentations 4:22 and Genesis 25:23 are implicit in the Hebrew text; I have supplied their addresses. The phrase 'the star that treads' (הכוכב הדורך) refers back to the preceding prophecy in Numbers 24:17 about the star from Jacob."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:08:29.132801642Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}